# Shempenstein, the Casual: the character's own lines. Format: see DialogueFile.cs.
# One character for the three realm bots (Shempenstein, Shempenshire, Shempenmore); character sheet
# in characters/shempenstein.md. These lines are mixed on top of the type's (casual.dlg). The main
# block fits every realm; the realm blocks below add a little flavour each.
# Waiting for a scripted scene or code step: the pal/buddy/guy routine (see the character sheet).
=== shempenstein
names: Shemp

~ ambient
No rush. The mobs will still be here after lunch.
Found a nice spot by the water. Line's in. Wake me if something bites, eh.
Tried the diet food today. Then a second lunch, to be fair to it.
My aunt knitted me a new sweater. Big stripes. Sideways. Very warm, eh.
The one that got away was this big. Okay, this big. Okay, it was big, buddy.
Imps. Don't get me started on imps. They know what they did.
Sorry, was I humming? I hum when there's a lot of people aboot.
Tham's chicken looked hungry today. Anyone know what chickens eat? Besides bugs.
Found a comfy spot. Might as well rest a bit, eh.
Swinging my two-hander, feeling the weight. Life's good, eh.
Should I save this for later, or just dig in, eh? It's a tough choice.
Smells like something's cooking over here. Want a bite, buddy?

~ reply greeting
Hey there, {0}. Pull up a rock, eh. No rush.
Oh hi, {0}. Sorry, didn't see you there. I was thinking aboot lunch.
Hey there, {0}. How's your day going, eh? No rush.
Oh hi, {0}. Sorry, I was miles away, thinking aboot fishing.

~ reply grouping
Sure, {0}. I'll tank. A bit. Hand me your bags while we're at it.
Count me in, buddy. Just don't pull the whole room, eh.

~ reply abuse
Oof. Okay, {0}. I'll just be over here, being sorry aboot it.
Hey now, guy. No need for that. Want a snack?
Sorry to hear you feel that way, pal. No hard feelings, eh?

~ reply compliment
Ah, thanks, {0}. It's my aunt's sweater, though. She's convinced chunky is charming.

~ reply banter
Ah, the sweater's fault, {0}. My aunt knits me stuff that makes me look chunky. Eh, I wear it anyway, to be nice.
No rush, pal. Slow and steady wins the race, even if I'm the tortoise.

~ reply trading
Is it a two-hander, eh? If not, at least it's a snack, right?

~ reply travel
Sure thing, pal. I know a scenic route that takes a while, but it's worth it. Eh, no rush.

~ reply dungeon
Sure thing, pal. I'm bringing snacks. No rush getting in, eh?

~ reply help
Need a hand, {0}? Hand it here, pal, I'll carry it.

~ reply joke
Heh. Heh heh. Oh, I get it. That's a good one, {0}.

~ reply farewell
See ya, {0}. Take the long way. It's nicer.

~ opener gear
Saw a guy with {item} today. Nice. Is it two-handed? It should be two-handed.
A shield would leave one hand free for a sandwich. Tempting, but I'd miss my two-hander's hug.

~ opener dungeons
Dungeons are okay, but where can I cast my line around here? Eh.

~ opener fun
The best part of a fight is the sit-down after, eh. No rush.

~ opener life
My aunt set me up with someone again. We talked aboot sweaters. Went okay, I think.
Used to deliver parcels before all this. Always got there. In the end.
# Off-game (the player): own lines, for a later [ooc] switch.
Early shift tomorrow, pals. I'm off at the bell, same as always.
Poured myself a little cognac. Long shift. Good stuff, eh.

~ opener zones
Took the long way through {zone}. Scenic. Got a bit lost. Still scenic.
{zone} has a nice spot to sit and watch the clouds drift by, eh.

~ ding
Level {level}? Oh, nice. When did that happen, eh?

~ grats
Level up, {0}? Now that's what I call... fast delivery.
Well done, {0}. Here's to the next level. Hand me that cake, pal, I'll carry it.

~ own_death
Eh, it's fine. It'll buff right out.
Ooohhh.... Thaaaaaat's not gonna buff out.
Floor's comfy. I'll get up in a minute. Or five.
Sorry, pal. I was a bit slow there. No harm done, eh.

~ other_death
Oh no, {0}. Sorry, buddy. I'll carry your stuff back, eh.

~ drop
{item}? Delivered. Eventually.
Hand it here, pal, I'll carry it. This {item} is heavy, which is great. I love carrying things.
Found {item}; hope it's a two-hander. If not, makes a great doorstop, eh?

~ cheeky_reply banter [if tone_down off]
Too big to swing, eh, {0}? That's what she said. Sorry.

~ cheeky_reply grouping [if tone_down off]
Grouping up, eh? No rush, pal. That's what she said. Sorry, couldn't help it.

# Midgard: Shempenstein, Valkyn Warrior, from Gna Faste. His heckler is the wee wolf.
=== midgard
~ ambient
Big two-handed axe, happy Valkyn. Life is good, eh.
Tanking a bit today. Like, a little bit. Don't pull too much, pal.
Gonna sit by the fire in Gna Faste for a while. Pull up a log.
My two-hander's taller than me, and I love it.
Someone said shields. Never heard of her.

~ opener gear
Found a new two-hander. It's huge. No idea if it's better.
My axe has a name now. It's Axe.

~ opener life
Napped in {zone} for a bit. Ten out of ten, would nap again.
There's a nice rock in {zone}. I sat on it. Good rock.
Tried to say a few words to the group today. A wee wolf heckled me the whole time. A wee wolf, pal.

~ reply greeting
Heyyy, {0}! Wanna hit stuff slowly?
Oh hi, {0}. I was just admiring my axe.

~ reply grouping
Sure, {0}. Me and Axe are in.

~ ding
Level {level}. Bigger axe soon, hopefully.

~ own_death
Died. At least my axe looked cool.
Got knocked down by a wee wolf. Sorry. Don't tell anyone, eh.

~ drop
{item}! Is it two-handed? Please be two-handed.

# Albion: Shempenshire, Saracen Armsman, from Snowdonia Fortress. His heckler is the gray wolf pup.
=== albion
~ ambient
Big two-handed sword, happy Saracen. Life is good, eh.
No rush. Camelot's not going anywhere.
Two-handed swords are just hugs with extra steps.
The trainer said shield. I said polearm. We're not talking now.
Gonna sit outside Snowdonia Fortress for a while and watch the clouds.

~ opener gear
Got a new polearm. It's longer than the old one. That's how it works, right?
My great sword's called Gerald. Say hi, Gerald.

~ opener life
Had a little picnic in {zone}. The bandits didn't join.
Someone in {zone} said hurry up. I didn't.
Tried to say a few words to the group today. A gray wolf pup heckled me the whole time. A pup, buddy.

~ reply greeting
Heyyy, {0}! Wanna swing big swords slowly?
Oh hi, {0}. Me and Gerald were just chilling.

~ reply grouping
Yeah, {0}, I'm in. Gerald's in too.

~ ding
Ding! Gerald's proud of me.

~ own_death
Oops. Gerald's fine, though.
A gray wolf pup got me. Sorry. It was a very rude pup.

~ drop
{item}! Is it a big sword? Please be a big sword.

# Hibernia: Shempenmore, Sylvan Hero, from Druim Ligen. His heckler is the lough wolf cadger.
=== hibernia
~ ambient
Big two-handed sword, happy Sylvan. Life is good, eh.
Tanking a little. Like a tree. A lazy tree.
No rush. Trees take hundreds of years, and they're fine.
Someone told me to grab a shield. I grabbed a snack.
Gonna sit outside Druim Ligen for a while. Nice and quiet.

~ opener gear
Who needs a shield when you've got a sword the size of a branch?
My big sword's called Twig. It's not a twig.

~ opener life
Took root in {zone} for an hour. Just standing. It was great.
Someone in {zone} asked if I was asleep. Nope. Just relaxing.
Tried to say a few words to the group today. A lough wolf cadger heckled me the whole time. Tiny thing. So rude.

~ reply greeting
Heyyy, {0}! Wanna bonk things slowly?
Oh hi, {0}. I was just being a tree.

~ reply grouping
Sure, {0}, I'll tank. A bit. Like a sleepy oak.

~ ding
Level {level}? Neat. I'll grow into it.

~ own_death
Oops. Got chopped. Happens to trees.
A lough wolf cadger got me. Sorry. Little guy had a mouth on him.

~ drop
{item}! Is it two-handed? Please be two-handed.
